<title>USA: Noble studying methanol plant feasibility.</title>
<headline>Noble studying methanol plant feasibility.</headline>
<dateline>ARDMORE, Okla. 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Noble Affiliates Inc said Tuesday its subsidiary Samedan Oil Corp had entered into an agreement with Raytheon Co's Raytheon Engineers and Construction to prepare budget cost estimates for use in evaluating the feasibility of erecting a 2,500-metric-tonne-per-day methanol plant on the island of Bioko, Equatorial Guinea, off the west coast of Africa.</p>
<p>The plant would be built to use natural gas from the Alba field, in which Samedan owns a 34.7 percent working interest.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
